7. Active leptomeningeal disease or poorly controlled brain metastases. Patients with suspected or confirmed brain metastases are allowed to be enrolled if they have no obvious symptoms and the results of imaging examinations performed at least 28 days before the first dose of the study drug showed stable disease and no treatment (e.g., radiotherapy, surgery, or corticosteroid treatment) is required to control the symptoms of brain metastases within 28 days before the first dose of the study drug;
